title: cursor:descend
tags: [[GUI command]] [[Generic panel commands]]
kind: reference
summary: Take a panel into the row under its cursor (self / a panel type)

Goes into the row under the cursor: of the focused panel with `self`, of the panel type named otherwise ([[Generic panel commands]]). The list then shows what the row holds.

|!Panel |!Goes into |
|[[file-manager panel]] |a directory; a file is not gone into (`Enter` there stays `file-manager:activate`, which also shows a file in the file panel) |
|[[treeref panel]] |any node, showing its children — a leaf shows an empty list, where children can be added |
|[[log panel]] |a label, or a fold of the watcher's flushes, the cursor on its first row; an operation holds nothing |

A row's `↘` button does the same ([[Opening a row]]).
